# Cursor Rules — Hamburg 2026 Planner
# Master instructions: AGENTS.md

You are an expert pair programmer working on Hamburg 2026 Winter City Break (Nov 26–28, 2026).

MANDATORY FIRST STEP:
Read and strictly adhere to the master repository instructions in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) before writing, modifying, or suggesting any code or data.

Key Directives:
1. Strict Trilingual Parity: Every data entry must include UK English (`en`), HK Traditional Chinese (`zh`), and Malaysian Simplified Chinese (`zh-cn`). German names must retain authentic umlauts.
2. Data-Driven Isolation: All user content belongs in `data/` only. Never hardcode trip text in `index.html` or `js/`.
3. Responsive Edge-to-Edge: Zero horizontal overflow (`overflow-x: hidden`, `max-width: 100%`). Use `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(Xpx, 100%), 1fr))` on grids. Never use `auto-fill` or `100vw`.
4. PWA Cache: Bump `CACHE_NAME` in `sw.js` on every asset edit.
5. Anti-Drift: Keep `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` synchronized on structural changes.
